WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:05.153
- [Narrator] It was the game that

00:00:05.153 --> 00:00:06.560
coined a dozen catch-phrases.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:07.760
- [Commentator In Game] Boomshakalaka!

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:10.389
- [Narrator] And made over a
billion dollars in quarters.

00:00:10.389 --> 00:00:11.880
- [Commentator In Game] Jams it in!

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.061
- [Narrator] But NBA Jam almost
never saw the light of day.

00:00:14.061 --> 00:00:17.750
- [Commentator In Game]
Oh my, he's on fire!

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:21.333
- [Commentator In Game]
Welcome to NBA Jam.

00:00:23.392 --> 00:00:25.664
- [Narrator] This is NBA Jam
game-designer, Mark Turmell.

00:00:25.664 --> 00:00:28.704
- So we put together a
demo, a video tape, VHS.

00:00:28.704 --> 00:00:30.093
We sent it to the NBA and said,

00:00:30.093 --> 00:00:31.907
'Hey we're making this cool game'

00:00:31.907 --> 00:00:33.195
and they immediately shut it down and said

00:00:33.195 --> 00:00:37.096
'No, we don't want the
NBA logo in the arcades.’

00:00:37.096 --> 00:00:40.347
So, once we got rejected
we made a video tape

00:00:40.347 --> 00:00:42.645
of nice family entertainment centers

00:00:42.645 --> 00:00:44.593
and we sent that back to them and said,

00:00:44.593 --> 00:00:47.295
'Look, you know, your logo can be here,’

00:00:47.295 --> 00:00:50.795
so they relented and, uh, provided the license.

00:00:51.816 --> 00:00:54.365
When we put it in the arcade
for the very first time

00:00:54.365 --> 00:00:57.347
there were no stats that
differentiated the players.

00:00:57.347 --> 00:01:00.925
Everybody assumed that Shaq
was a bad three-point shooter

00:01:00.925 --> 00:01:02.976
or Stockton could steal the ball,

00:01:02.976 --> 00:01:04.496
so we realized pretty quickly

00:01:04.496 --> 00:01:06.627
that we had to, you know, up our game

00:01:06.627 --> 00:01:09.045
to match the real world.

00:01:09.045 --> 00:01:10.187
- [Commentator In Game] No good.

00:01:10.187 --> 00:01:12.164
- Well, if it's just
looking at pure attributes,

00:01:12.164 --> 00:01:14.314
I happen to be the best
player in the game.

00:01:14.314 --> 00:01:15.635
- [Commentator In Game] Showtime!

00:01:15.635 --> 00:01:17.336
- When you actually put
in my secret character

00:01:17.336 --> 00:01:20.096
it just shows question marks for the stats,

00:01:20.096 --> 00:01:22.467
but they're all tens or nines.

00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:24.205
- [Commentator In Game] Take that.

00:01:24.205 --> 00:01:25.635
- [Commentator In Game]
From the outside, count it.

00:01:25.635 --> 00:01:27.243
- I'm pretty good at NBA Jam.

00:01:27.243 --> 00:01:28.265
- [Narrator] To test the claim,

00:01:28.265 --> 00:01:29.638
we had Mark hack into the machine

00:01:29.638 --> 00:01:30.527
- [Mark] There we go.

00:01:30.527 --> 00:01:32.189
- [Narrator] And turn on cheat codes.

00:01:32.189 --> 00:01:35.189
- [Mark] Alright, now we're talking.

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:41.355
Usually, when somebody finds
out that I made NBA Jam

00:01:41.355 --> 00:01:44.717
they say 'I spent so much
money on that NBA Jam'

00:01:44.717 --> 00:01:47.397
or you know, 'I flunked a class in college

00:01:47.397 --> 00:01:49.218
because of NBA Jam.'

00:01:49.218 --> 00:01:50.051
- [Commentator In Game] Kaboom.

00:01:50.051 --> 00:01:52.597
- But I look at the game
now, I wish it were smoother,

00:01:52.597 --> 00:01:54.309
but it was the technology at the time.

00:01:54.309 --> 00:01:55.477
- [Commentator In Game] Razzle dazzle.

00:01:55.477 --> 00:01:57.069
- The game still holds up today.

00:01:57.069 --> 00:02:01.236
- [Commentator In Game]
It is (buzzer) good!

